{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-76747","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139692","text":"κ Integration Spec: Product-Level Specification"}]},{"id":"blk-76748","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139693","text":"Version 0.2.0 — Normalized"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76750","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139694","text":"How the cyclicity invariant κ is computed, surfaced, and used across Graphonomous, BendScript, Deliberatic, TickTickClock, and the [&] Protocol.  "},{"id":"spn-139695","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.2.0 changes (from Codex review):"},{"id":"spn-139696","text":" - Normalized all field names to a single canonical schema (§2.4) - Resolved tool naming: "},{"id":"spn-139697","marks":["code"],"text":"analyze_topology"},{"id":"spn-139698","text":" is the standalone tool; "},{"id":"spn-139699","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-139700","text":" gains a "},{"id":"spn-139701","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-139702","text":" field — no "},{"id":"spn-139703","marks":["code"],"text":"memory_recall_with_topology"},{"id":"spn-139704","text":" tool - Fixed approximation representation: "},{"id":"spn-139705","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-139706","text":" is always an integer; large SCCs add "},{"id":"spn-139707","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-139708","text":" (no "},{"id":"spn-139709","marks":["code"],"text":"exact"},{"id":"spn-139710","text":" field) - Added instrumentation requirements (§7) - Clarified BendScript directed-edge policy (§4.3)"}]}],"id":"blk-76749","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-76751","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139711","text":"1. Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-76752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139712","text":"κ (kappa) is a graph-theoretic invariant that measures the minimum irreducible bidirectional information flow in a directed graph. It is the routing primitive that determines whether a query region of a knowledge graph requires single-pass retrieval (κ = 0) or iterative deliberation (κ > 0)."}]},{"id":"blk-76753","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139713","text":"This spec defines:"}]},{"id":"blk-76754","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76756","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139714","text":"How κ is computed"}]}],"id":"blk-76755","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76758","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139715","text":"Where it is computed in the stack"}]}],"id":"blk-76757","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139716","text":"How it routes inference"}]}],"id":"blk-76759","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76762","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139717","text":"How it is surfaced to users"}]}],"id":"blk-76761","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76764","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139718","text":"How it integrates with each product"}]}],"id":"blk-76763","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76765","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139719","text":"2. Computation"}]},{"id":"blk-76766","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139720","text":"2.1 Algorithm"}]},{"id":"blk-76767","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function compute_kappa(graph):\n    # Pre-step: define node universe U from the analyzed subgraph/query result.\n    # Ignore any edge where src ∉ U or dst ∉ U.\n    # Exclude self-loops (u -> u) from adjacency for κ computation.\n    # Step 1: Find all strongly connected components\n    sccs = tarjan_scc(graph)                    # O(V + E)\n\n    # Step 2: For each nontrivial SCC (size > 1)\n    results = []\n    for scc in sccs where |scc| > 1:\n        # Step 3: Enumerate bipartitions, find minimum bidirectional cut\n        k = infinity\n        for (A, B) in nontrivial_bipartitions(scc):\n            edges_a_to_b = count_edges(A, B, graph)\n            edges_b_to_a = count_edges(B, A, graph)\n            bidirectional_cut = min(edges_a_to_b, edges_b_to_a)\n            k = min(k, bidirectional_cut)\n            if k == 0: break  # early exit (can't go lower)\n\n        # Step 4: Record SCC with its κ value and minimum-cut partition\n        results.append({\n            scc: scc,\n            kappa: k,\n            min_cut_partition: (A_min, B_min),\n            min_cut_edges: edges_achieving_minimum\n        })\n\n    return results"},{"id":"blk-76768","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139721","text":"2.2 Complexity"}]},{"id":"blk-76769","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139722","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCC decomposition:"},{"id":"spn-139723","text":" O(V + E) via Tarjan's algorithm"}]}],"id":"blk-76770","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76773","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139724","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ computation per SCC:"},{"id":"spn-139725","text":" O(2^|SCC| × |SCC|²) in the worst case (enumerating all bipartitions)"}]}],"id":"blk-76772","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76775","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139726","marks":["bold"],"text":"Practical constraint:"},{"id":"spn-139727","text":" For SCCs up to ~20 nodes, bipartition enumeration is feasible in real time. For larger SCCs, use approximation:"}]}],"id":"blk-76774","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139728","text":"Return SCC size as a proxy for κ, with "},{"id":"spn-139729","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-139730","text":" flag"}]}],"id":"blk-76776","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139731","text":"κ field remains an integer (the estimate), never a symbol/atom/string"}]}],"id":"blk-76778","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139732","marks":["bold"],"text":"Node-universe rule (NORMATIVE):"},{"id":"spn-139733","text":" Analyze only the node set supplied by retrieval/query scope (or explicit "},{"id":"spn-139734","marks":["code"],"text":"node_ids"},{"id":"spn-139735","text":" input). Do not pull in external nodes implicitly during κ analysis."}]}],"id":"blk-76780","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139736","marks":["bold"],"text":"Self-loop rule (NORMATIVE):"},{"id":"spn-139737","text":" Exclude self-loops ("},{"id":"spn-139738","marks":["code"],"text":"source == target"},{"id":"spn-139739","text":") from κ adjacency and cut counts."}]}],"id":"blk-76782","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76784","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139740","text":"2.3 Incremental Updates"}]},{"id":"blk-76785","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139741","text":"When an edge is added or removed from the knowledge graph:"}]},{"id":"blk-76786","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76788","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139742","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge addition:"},{"id":"spn-139743","text":" Can only merge SCCs or enlarge existing ones. Re-run Tarjan on the affected component. If a new nontrivial SCC is formed, compute κ for it."}]}],"id":"blk-76787","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76790","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139744","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge removal:"},{"id":"spn-139745","text":" Can only split SCCs or shrink them. Re-run Tarjan on the affected component. Recompute κ for any remaining nontrivial SCCs."}]}],"id":"blk-76789","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76792","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139746","marks":["bold"],"text":"Optimization:"},{"id":"spn-139747","text":" Maintain an SCC index alongside the knowledge graph. Incremental SCC algorithms (e.g., Bender, Fineman & Gilbert 2015) can update SCCs in O(V) amortized per edge change."}]}],"id":"blk-76791","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-76793","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139748","text":"2.4 Canonical Schema (NORMATIVE — all implementations must match)"}]},{"id":"blk-76794","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139749","text":"Every κ topology result — whether from Elixir, JavaScript, or MCP JSON — uses these exact field names:"}]},{"id":"blk-76795","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"sccs\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scc-0\",\n      \"nodes\": [\"node-a\", \"node-b\"],\n      \"kappa\": 2,\n      \"approximate\": false,\n      \"fault_line_edges\": [\n        {\"source\": \"node-a\", \"target\": \"node-b\"}\n      ],\n      \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n      \"deliberation_budget\": {\n        \"max_iterations\": 3,\n        \"agent_count\": 2,\n        \"timeout_multiplier\": 2.0,\n        \"confidence_threshold\": 0.80\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dag_nodes\": [\"node-x\", \"node-y\"],\n  \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n  \"max_kappa\": 2,\n  \"scc_count\": 1\n}"},{"id":"blk-76796","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139750","marks":["bold"],"text":"Field name rules (resolves all drift):"}]},{"id":"blk-76797","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76799","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139751","text":"Top-level routing key: "},{"id":"spn-139752","marks":["code"],"text":"routing"},{"id":"spn-139753","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-139754","marks":["code"],"text":"overall_routing"},{"id":"spn-139755","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-76798","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76801","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139756","text":"Edge endpoints: "},{"id":"spn-139757","marks":["code"],"text":"source"},{"id":"spn-139758","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-139759","marks":["code"],"text":"target"},{"id":"spn-139760","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-139761","marks":["code"],"text":"from"},{"id":"spn-139762","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-139763","marks":["code"],"text":"to"},{"id":"spn-139764","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-139765","marks":["code"],"text":"a"},{"id":"spn-139766","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-139767","marks":["code"],"text":"b"},{"id":"spn-139768","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-76800","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76803","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139769","text":"Fault lines: "},{"id":"spn-139770","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-139771","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-139772","marks":["code"],"text":"min_cut_edges"},{"id":"spn-139773","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-76802","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76805","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139774","text":"κ type: always "},{"id":"spn-139775","marks":["code"],"text":"integer"},{"id":"spn-139776","text":" (never string, atom, or symbol)"}]}],"id":"blk-76804","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76807","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139777","text":"Approximation: "},{"id":"spn-139778","marks":["code"],"text":"\"approximate\": true"},{"id":"spn-139779","text":" boolean flag on the SCC object; "},{"id":"spn-139780","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-139781","text":" still holds the integer estimate"}]}],"id":"blk-76806","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76809","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139782","text":"Routing values: "},{"id":"spn-139783","marks":["code"],"text":"\"fast\""},{"id":"spn-139784","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-139785","marks":["code"],"text":"\"deliberate\""},{"id":"spn-139786","text":" (strings in JSON, atoms "},{"id":"spn-139787","marks":["code"],"text":":fast"},{"id":"spn-139788","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-139789","marks":["code"],"text":":deliberate"},{"id":"spn-139790","text":" in Elixir, strings in JS)"}]}],"id":"blk-76808","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139791","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema boundary rules (NORMATIVE):"}]},{"id":"blk-76811","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76813","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139792","marks":["bold"],"text":"On MCP/JSON boundaries:"},{"id":"spn-139793","text":" use canonical snake_case keys exactly as defined in §2.4 ("},{"id":"spn-139794","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-139795","text":", "},{"id":"spn-139796","marks":["code"],"text":"max_kappa"},{"id":"spn-139797","text":", "},{"id":"spn-139798","marks":["code"],"text":"scc_count"},{"id":"spn-139799","text":", etc.)."}]}],"id":"blk-76812","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76815","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139800","marks":["bold"],"text":"Inside Elixir runtime:"},{"id":"spn-139801","text":" atoms are allowed for routing values ("},{"id":"spn-139802","marks":["code"],"text":":fast"},{"id":"spn-139803","text":", "},{"id":"spn-139804","marks":["code"],"text":":deliberate"},{"id":"spn-139805","text":"), but keys remain canonical and are serialized to JSON strings at the boundary."}]}],"id":"blk-76814","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76817","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139806","marks":["bold"],"text":"Inside JavaScript UI code:"},{"id":"spn-139807","text":" camelCase mirrors are allowed for local-only objects ("},{"id":"spn-139808","marks":["code"],"text":"faultLineEdges"},{"id":"spn-139809","text":", "},{"id":"spn-139810","marks":["code"],"text":"maxKappa"},{"id":"spn-139811","text":", "},{"id":"spn-139812","marks":["code"],"text":"sccCount"},{"id":"spn-139813","text":") for ergonomics, but any network payload or persisted topology record must be converted back to canonical snake_case."}]}],"id":"blk-76816","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139814","marks":["bold"],"text":"Elixir atom mapping:"}]},{"id":"blk-76819","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Elixir uses atoms internally, converts to strings for MCP JSON\n:fast       → \"fast\"\n:deliberate → \"deliberate\""},{"id":"blk-76820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139815","marks":["bold"],"text":"JavaScript mapping (local only):"}]},{"id":"blk-76821","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"// Local object ergonomics\n{ faultLineEdges, maxKappa, sccCount, routing }\n\n// MCP / wire payloads must remain canonical snake_case\n{ fault_line_edges, max_kappa, scc_count, routing }"},{"id":"blk-76822","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139816","text":"3. Routing Logic"}]},{"id":"blk-76823","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139817","text":"3.1 The κ Router"}]},{"id":"blk-76824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139818","text":"The κ router sits between memory retrieval and reasoning. It inspects the topological structure of the retrieved subgraph and makes a routing decision."}]},{"id":"blk-76825","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function kappa_route(retrieved_subgraph):\n    scc_analysis = compute_kappa(retrieved_subgraph)\n\n    dag_context = nodes NOT in any nontrivial SCC\n    scc_contexts = scc_analysis  # list of {scc, kappa, fault_line_edges, ...}\n\n    # DAG regions: single-pass retrieval\n    retrieval_context = topological_sort_and_collect(dag_context)\n\n    # SCC regions: flag for deliberation\n    deliberation_tasks = []\n    for scc_info in scc_contexts:\n        deliberation_tasks.append({\n            nodes: scc_info.scc,\n            kappa: scc_info.kappa,\n            fault_lines: scc_info.fault_line_edges,\n            budget: deliberation_budget(scc_info.kappa)\n        })\n\n    return {\n        retrieval_context: retrieval_context,\n        deliberation_tasks: deliberation_tasks,\n        routing: \"fast\" if len(deliberation_tasks) == 0 else \"deliberate\"\n    }"},{"id":"blk-76826","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139819","text":"3.2 Deliberation Budget Function"}]},{"id":"blk-76827","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139820","text":"The deliberation budget maps κ to concrete inference parameters. This is an engineering heuristic (not proved — to be tuned empirically). Caps on "},{"id":"spn-139821","marks":["code"],"text":"max_iterations"},{"id":"spn-139822","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-139823","marks":["code"],"text":"confidence_threshold"},{"id":"spn-139824","text":" are required to prevent runaway values when "},{"id":"spn-139825","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-139826","text":" SCCs use size-based κ estimates:"}]},{"id":"blk-76828","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function deliberation_budget(kappa):\n    return {\n        max_iterations: min(kappa + 1, 4),\n        agent_count: min(kappa, 3),\n        timeout_multiplier: min(1.0 + 0.5*kappa, 3.5),\n        confidence_threshold: min(0.7 + 0.05*kappa, 0.95)\n    }"},{"id":"blk-76829","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139827","text":"3.3 The Fast Path vs. Deliberation Path"}]},{"id":"blk-76830","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  Query arrives   │\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  &memory.recall  │   Graphonomous retrieves relevant subgraph\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  κ Router        │   Compute SCCs, κ values\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n              ┌───────┴────────┐\n              │                │\n         κ = 0 (all DAG)    κ > 0 (has SCCs)\n              │                │\n              ▼                ▼\n       ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────────┐\n       │ Fast Path │    │  Deliberation │\n       │ single    │    │  &reason via  │\n       │ pass      │    │  Deliberatic  │\n       │ retrieval │    │  κ-informed   │\n       └─────┬────┘    │  budget       │\n             │         └──────┬───────┘\n             │                │\n             └───────┬────────┘\n                     │\n                     ▼\n             ┌──────────────┐\n             │  &memory.learn │   Results feed back into graph\n             └──────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-76831","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139828","text":"4. Product Integration"}]},{"id":"blk-76832","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139829","text":"4.1 Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-76833","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139830","marks":["bold"],"text":"Where κ lives:"},{"id":"spn-139831","text":" Computed at query time on the retrieved subgraph. Cached per SCC in the knowledge graph index; invalidated on edge changes."}]},{"id":"blk-76834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139832","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-76835","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139833","marks":["code"],"text":"Retriever.retrieve/2"},{"id":"spn-139834","text":" now returns a "},{"id":"spn-139835","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-139836","text":" key alongside existing "},{"id":"spn-139837","marks":["code"],"text":"results"},{"id":"spn-139838","text":", "},{"id":"spn-139839","marks":["code"],"text":"causal_context"},{"id":"spn-139840","text":", "},{"id":"spn-139841","marks":["code"],"text":"stats"}]}],"id":"blk-76836","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139842","text":"New module "},{"id":"spn-139843","marks":["code"],"text":"Graphonomous.Topology"},{"id":"spn-139844","text":" computes and returns the full SCC analysis for a given subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-76838","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76841","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139845","text":"New function "},{"id":"spn-139846","marks":["code"],"text":"Store.list_edges_between/1"},{"id":"spn-139847","text":" fetches edges within a node set"}]}],"id":"blk-76840","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139848","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool: `analyze_topology` (NEW standalone tool):"}]},{"id":"blk-76843","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"analyze_topology\",\n  \"description\": \"Compute topological structure (SCCs, κ values, routing decision) for a set of nodes in the knowledge graph.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"node_ids\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"description\": \"Node IDs to analyze. If omitted, analyzes the full graph.\"\n      },\n      \"query\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Optional query text. If provided, retrieves relevant nodes first, then analyzes their topology.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-76844","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139849","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool: `retrieve_context` (EXISTING — augmented with topology):"}]},{"id":"blk-76845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139850","text":"The existing "},{"id":"spn-139851","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-139852","text":" tool gains a "},{"id":"spn-139853","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-139854","text":" field in its response. No new tool name — same endpoint, richer response:"}]},{"id":"blk-76846","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"query\": \"company strategy\",\n  \"count\": 7,\n  \"results\": [\"...existing results...\"],\n  \"causal_context\": [\"...existing...\"],\n  \"stats\": {\"...existing...\"},\n  \"topology\": {\n    \"sccs\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"scc-0\",\n        \"nodes\": [\"market-share\", \"revenue\", \"r-and-d\", \"product-quality\", \"customer-retention\"],\n        \"kappa\": 1,\n        \"approximate\": false,\n        \"fault_line_edges\": [\n          {\"source\": \"product-quality\", \"target\": \"market-share\"}\n        ],\n        \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n        \"deliberation_budget\": {\n          \"max_iterations\": 2,\n          \"agent_count\": 1,\n          \"timeout_multiplier\": 1.5,\n          \"confidence_threshold\": 0.75\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"dag_nodes\": [\"founding-date\", \"ceo-name\", \"headquarters\"],\n    \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n    \"max_kappa\": 1,\n    \"scc_count\": 1\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-76847","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139855","text":"4.2 Deliberatic"}]},{"id":"blk-76848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139856","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-76849","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139857","text":"Accepts "},{"id":"spn-139858","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-139859","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-139860","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-139861","text":" as input parameters on its deliberation endpoint."}]}],"id":"blk-76850","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76853","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139862","text":"Uses "},{"id":"spn-139863","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-139864","text":" to set argumentation depth (number of rounds)."}]}],"id":"blk-76852","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139865","text":"Uses "},{"id":"spn-139866","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-139867","text":" (minimum-cut edges) to generate the initial propositions that agents must argue about — these are the critical bidirectional dependencies."}]}],"id":"blk-76854","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76856","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139868","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool additions:"}]},{"id":"blk-76857","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"deliberate_on_scc\",\n  \"description\": \"Run structured argumentation on a strongly connected knowledge cluster. Uses κ to set deliberation budget and fault lines to seed propositions.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"scc_nodes\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n      \"scc_edges\": { \"type\": \"array\" },\n      \"kappa\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n      \"fault_line_edges\": { \"type\": \"array\" },\n      \"governance\": { \"type\": \"object\" }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-76858","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139869","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key insight:"},{"id":"spn-139870","text":" Deliberatic doesn't need to know about graph theory. It receives a set of propositions (derived from fault lines), a budget (derived from κ), and it argues. The graph intelligence lives in Graphonomous; the argumentation intelligence lives in Deliberatic. κ is the handshake between them."}]},{"id":"blk-76859","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139871","text":"4.3 BendScript"}]},{"id":"blk-76860","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139872","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-76861","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139873","text":"Directed-Edge Policy (NORMATIVE)"}]},{"id":"blk-76862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139874","text":"BendScript edges have a "},{"id":"spn-139875","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-139876","text":" property. For κ computation, edge directionality is determined by kind:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-76864","spans":[{"id":"spn-139877","text":"Edge kind"}]},{"id":"blk-76865","spans":[{"id":"spn-139878","text":"Directionality for κ"}]},{"id":"blk-76866","spans":[{"id":"spn-139879","text":"Rationale"}]}],"id":"blk-76863","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-76867","spans":[{"id":"spn-139880","marks":["code"],"text":"causal"}]},{"id":"blk-76868","spans":[{"id":"spn-139881","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directed"},{"id":"spn-139882","text":" (a → b)"}]},{"id":"blk-76869","spans":[{"id":"spn-139883","text":"Cause precedes effect"}]}],[{"id":"blk-76870","spans":[{"id":"spn-139884","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal"}]},{"id":"blk-76871","spans":[{"id":"spn-139885","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directed"},{"id":"spn-139886","text":" (a → b)"}]},{"id":"blk-76872","spans":[{"id":"spn-139887","text":"Before precedes after"}]}],[{"id":"blk-76873","spans":[{"id":"spn-139888","marks":["code"],"text":"context"}]},{"id":"blk-76874","spans":[{"id":"spn-139889","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-139890","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-76875","spans":[{"id":"spn-139891","text":"Symmetric, no feedback"}]}],[{"id":"blk-76876","spans":[{"id":"spn-139892","marks":["code"],"text":"associative"}]},{"id":"blk-76877","spans":[{"id":"spn-139893","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-139894","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-76878","spans":[{"id":"spn-139895","text":"Symmetric, no feedback"}]}],[{"id":"blk-76879","spans":[{"id":"spn-139896","marks":["code"],"text":"user"}]},{"id":"blk-76880","spans":[{"id":"spn-139897","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-139898","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-76881","spans":[{"id":"spn-139899","text":"Ambiguous directionality"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-76882","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139900","text":"This is a "},{"id":"spn-139901","marks":["bold"],"text":"hard rule"},{"id":"spn-139902","text":", not a toggle. Only "},{"id":"spn-139903","marks":["code"],"text":"causal"},{"id":"spn-139904","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-139905","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal"},{"id":"spn-139906","text":" edges participate in SCC/κ computation. The filter constant:"}]},{"id":"blk-76883","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"const DIRECTED_KINDS = ['causal', 'temporal'];"},{"id":"blk-76884","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139907","text":"Visual Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-76885","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139908","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCC clusters rendered visually:"},{"id":"spn-139909","text":" Nodes within a nontrivial SCC share a colored halo or background region. Color intensity scales with κ."}]}],"id":"blk-76886","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139910","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minimum-cut edges highlighted:"},{"id":"spn-139911","text":" Fault-line edges rendered in dashed style ("},{"id":"spn-139912","marks":["code"],"text":"ctx.setLineDash([6, 4])"},{"id":"spn-139913","text":") with brighter color."}]}],"id":"blk-76888","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139914","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ badge on SCC clusters:"},{"id":"spn-139915","text":" Each SCC cluster shows its κ value as a small badge, e.g., \"κ=2\"."}]}],"id":"blk-76890","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76892","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139916","text":"Interaction Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-76893","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139917","marks":["bold"],"text":"Topology preview via context menu:"},{"id":"spn-139918","text":" When the user right-clicks a node and selects \"Connect to…\" (a new context menu item), BendScript shows candidate target nodes with topology impact annotations:"}]}],"id":"blk-76894","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139919","text":"\"→ NodeX: creates feedback loop (κ: 0→1)\""}]}],"id":"blk-76896","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76899","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139920","text":"\"→ NodeY: strengthens loop (κ: 1→2)\""}]}],"id":"blk-76898","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139921","text":"\"→ NodeZ: no topological change\""}]}],"id":"blk-76900","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139922","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Bend\" action:"},{"id":"spn-139923","text":" Right-click context menu on DAG nodes — automatically suggests the nearest edge that would create a feedback loop."}]}],"id":"blk-76902","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76905","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139924","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Unbend\" action:"},{"id":"spn-139925","text":" Right-click context menu on SCC nodes — identifies the fault-line edge and offers to remove it."}]}],"id":"blk-76904","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139926","marks":["bold"],"text":"Note:"},{"id":"spn-139927","text":" BendScript does NOT currently have drag-to-connect edge creation. The topology preview is accessed via the context menu \"Connect to…\" flow. Do not implement drag-to-connect in this phase."}]},{"id":"blk-76907","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139928","text":"HUD"}]},{"id":"blk-76908","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76910","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139929","marks":["bold"],"text":"Global κ display:"},{"id":"spn-139930","text":" The existing HUD gains a κ readout showing the maximum κ across all SCCs in the graph, and a count of SCCs."}]}],"id":"blk-76909","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139931","marks":["bold"],"text":"Routing indicator:"},{"id":"spn-139932","text":" \"mode: RETRIEVAL\" (all κ = 0) or \"mode: DELIBERATION\" (any κ > 0)."}]}],"id":"blk-76911","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76913","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139933","text":"4.4 The [&] Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-76914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139934","marks":["bold"],"text":"Grammar extension:"}]},{"id":"blk-76915","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"# Extended [&] capability grammar — topology-aware routing\nTopologyOp      := \"&topology\" \".\" (\"analyze\" | \"route\" | \"kappa\")\n\n# Updated pipeline pattern\nInferencePipeline :=\n    \"&memory.recall\" \"(\" QueryExpr \")\"\n    \"|>\" \"&topology.analyze\" \"()\"\n    \"|>\" \"&topology.route\" \"()\"\n    \"|>\" \"&reason.deliberate\" \"(\" \"budget:\" \":κ\" \")\"\n    \"|>\" \"&memory.learn\" \"()\""},{"id":"blk-76916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139935","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema extension (ampersand.schema.json):"}]},{"id":"blk-76917","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"&topology.analyze\": {\n      \"provider\": \"graphonomous\",\n      \"description\": \"Compute SCC decomposition and κ values for a subgraph\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"max_scc_size_for_exact\": 20,\n        \"approximation_strategy\": \"scc_size_proxy\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"&topology.route\": {\n      \"provider\": \"builtin\",\n      \"description\": \"Route inference based on κ: DAG regions → fast path, SCC regions → deliberation\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"deliberation_provider\": \"deliberatic\",\n        \"fast_path_provider\": \"graphonomous\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-76918","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139936","text":"4.5 TickTickClock"}]},{"id":"blk-76919","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139937","marks":["bold"],"text":"Connection:"},{"id":"spn-139938","text":" For discrete time-series dynamics, the transition graph of the system has κ > 0 if and only if the system has a periodic orbit. TickTickClock can use this as a formal periodicity detector:"}]},{"id":"blk-76920","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139939","text":"Discretize time-series data into state transitions"}]}],"id":"blk-76921","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76924","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139940","text":"Build the transition graph"}]}],"id":"blk-76923","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76926","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139941","text":"Compute κ"}]}],"id":"blk-76925","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76928","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139942","text":"κ > 0 → periodic pattern detected, flag for temporal reasoning"}]}],"id":"blk-76927","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76930","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139943","text":"κ = 0 → pure drift, no recurrence"}]}],"id":"blk-76929","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76931","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139944","text":"This is a secondary integration (TickTickClock already has Mamba SSM for pattern detection), but it provides a complementary structural signal."}]},{"id":"blk-76932","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139945","text":"4.6 OpenSentience"}]},{"id":"blk-76933","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139946","marks":["bold"],"text":"Role:"},{"id":"spn-139947","text":" Research home for the theoretical foundations. Hosts:"}]},{"id":"blk-76934","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76936","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139948","text":"The κ paper (theoretical background, proofs, categorical framework)"}]}],"id":"blk-76935","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76938","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139949","text":"The proof code (runnable verification)"}]}],"id":"blk-76937","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76940","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139950","text":"Interactive demos (live κ computation on user-constructed graphs)"}]}],"id":"blk-76939","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76942","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139951","text":"The original Scale Topology Axis essay (broader theoretical context connecting κ to physics, cosmology, and consciousness science)"}]}],"id":"blk-76941","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76943","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139952","text":"5. Implementation Priority"}]},{"id":"blk-76944","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139953","text":"Phase 1: Core (ship first)"}]},{"id":"blk-76945","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76947","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139954","text":"[ ] Port κ computation to Elixir (Graphonomous server-side)"}]}],"id":"blk-76946","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76949","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139955","text":"[ ] Port κ computation to JavaScript (BendScript client-side)"}]}],"id":"blk-76948","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76951","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139956","text":"[ ] Integrate Tarjan's SCC into Graphonomous's graph index"}]}],"id":"blk-76950","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76953","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139957","text":"[ ] Return topology annotations from "},{"id":"spn-139958","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"}]}],"id":"blk-76952","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76955","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139959","text":"[ ] Add SCC visualization to BendScript canvas"}]}],"id":"blk-76954","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76956","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139960","text":"Phase 2: Routing (ship second)"}]},{"id":"blk-76957","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76959","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139961","text":"[ ] Implement κ router in the [&] pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-76958","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76961","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139962","text":"[ ] Connect κ router to Deliberatic trigger"}]}],"id":"blk-76960","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76963","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139963","text":"[ ] Add deliberation budget function"}]}],"id":"blk-76962","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76965","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139964","text":"[ ] Test on real knowledge graph queries: does κ-aware routing improve answer quality?"}]}],"id":"blk-76964","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76966","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139965","text":"Phase 3: Polish (ship third)"}]},{"id":"blk-76967","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139966","text":"[ ] BendScript topology preview via context menu"}]}],"id":"blk-76968","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76971","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139967","text":"[ ] Bend/Unbend context menu actions"}]}],"id":"blk-76970","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76973","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139968","text":"[ ] HUD κ display and routing indicator"}]}],"id":"blk-76972","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76975","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139969","text":"[ ] TickTickClock periodicity detection via κ"}]}],"id":"blk-76974","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76977","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139970","text":"[ ] OpenSentience publication of κ paper and demos"}]}],"id":"blk-76976","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76978","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139971","text":"Phase 4: Optimization"}]},{"id":"blk-76979","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76981","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139972","text":"[ ] Incremental SCC maintenance (avoid full recomputation on every edge change)"}]}],"id":"blk-76980","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139973","text":"[ ] Approximate κ for large SCCs (> 20 nodes)"}]}],"id":"blk-76982","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76985","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139974","text":"[ ] Benchmark: latency impact of topology computation on query path"}]}],"id":"blk-76984","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-76987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-139975","text":"[ ] A/B test: κ-routed inference vs. uniform retrieval on quality metrics"}]}],"id":"blk-76986","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-76988","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-139976","text":"6. Success Metrics"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-76990","spans":[{"id":"spn-139977","text":"Metric"}]},{"id":"blk-76991","spans":[{"id":"spn-139978","text":"Baseline (no κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-76992","spans":[{"id":"spn-139979","text":"Target (with κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-76993","spans":[{"id":"spn-139980","text":"How to Measure"}]}],"id":"blk-76989","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-76994","spans":[{"id":"spn-139981","text":"Answer coherence on circular topics"}]},{"id":"blk-76995","spans":[{"id":"spn-139982","text":"Human eval ~60%"}]},{"id":"blk-76996","spans":[{"id":"spn-139983","text":"Human eval ~80%"}]},{"id":"blk-76997","spans":[{"id":"spn-139984","text":"Blind eval on queries touching SCCs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-76998","spans":[{"id":"spn-139985","text":"Unnecessary deliberation calls"}]},{"id":"blk-76999","spans":[{"id":"spn-139986","text":"N/A (no routing)"}]},{"id":"blk-77000","spans":[{"id":"spn-139987","text":"< 20% of queries"}]},{"id":"blk-77001","spans":[{"id":"spn-139988","text":"Track κ=0 queries that hit deliberation anyway"}]}],[{"id":"blk-77002","spans":[{"id":"spn-139989","text":"Deliberation convergence speed"}]},{"id":"blk-77003","spans":[{"id":"spn-139990","text":"Fixed rounds"}]},{"id":"blk-77004","spans":[{"id":"spn-139991","text":"κ+1 rounds avg"}]},{"id":"blk-77005","spans":[{"id":"spn-139992","text":"Measure rounds to convergence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-77006","spans":[{"id":"spn-139993","text":"User engagement in BendScript"}]},{"id":"blk-77007","spans":[{"id":"spn-139994","text":"Nodes/edges per session"}]},{"id":"blk-77008","spans":[{"id":"spn-139995","text":"+30%"}]},{"id":"blk-77009","spans":[{"id":"spn-139996","text":"Track topology actions (bend/unbend/stargate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-77010","spans":[{"id":"spn-139997","text":"OpenSentience traffic"}]},{"id":"blk-77011","spans":[{"id":"spn-139998","text":"Baseline"}]},{"id":"blk-77012","spans":[{"id":"spn-139999","text":"Organic from dev community"}]},{"id":"blk-77013","spans":[{"id":"spn-140000","text":"Track referrals from product UIs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-77014","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-140001","text":"7. Instrumentation Requirements (NEW in v0.2.0)"}]},{"id":"blk-77015","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140002","text":"All κ computation must emit telemetry. This is required for Gate C (performance) and Gate D (product effect) validation."}]},{"id":"blk-77016","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-140003","text":"7.1 Latency Counters (Elixir — "},{"id":"spn-140004","marks":["code"],"text":":telemetry"},{"id":"spn-140005","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-77017","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Emit on every topology computation\n# REQUIRED UNIT: duration_ms (float milliseconds)\n# If measured via :timer.tc/1, convert with: duration_ms = duration_us / 1000.0\n:telemetry.execute(\n  [:graphonomous, :topology, :analyze],\n  %{duration_ms: elapsed_ms, node_count: n, edge_count: e},\n  %{scc_count: scc_count, max_kappa: max_kappa, routing: routing}\n)"},{"id":"blk-77018","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140006","text":"Track:"}]},{"id":"blk-77019","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77021","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140007","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.duration_ms"},{"id":"spn-140008","text":" — p50, p95, p99 (canonical latency metric)"}]}],"id":"blk-77020","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77023","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140009","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.node_count"},{"id":"spn-140010","text":" — distribution of subgraph sizes"}]}],"id":"blk-77022","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77025","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140011","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.edge_count"},{"id":"spn-140012","text":" — distribution of subgraph densities"}]}],"id":"blk-77024","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77027","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140013","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.scc_count"},{"id":"spn-140014","text":" — how often SCCs are found"}]}],"id":"blk-77026","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77029","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140015","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.routing.deliberate_ratio"},{"id":"spn-140016","text":" — deliberate / total analyzes"}]}],"id":"blk-77028","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77031","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140017","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.self_loop_filtered_count"},{"id":"spn-140018","text":" — number of self-loops ignored during adjacency construction"}]}],"id":"blk-77030","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-77032","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-140019","text":"7.2 Routing Decision Counters"}]},{"id":"blk-77033","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":":telemetry.execute(\n  [:graphonomous, :topology, :route],\n  %{},\n  %{decision: :fast | :deliberate, max_kappa: max_kappa, trigger: :retrieve_context | :analyze_topology}\n)"},{"id":"blk-77034","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140020","text":"Track:"}]},{"id":"blk-77035","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77037","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140021","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.fast_count"},{"id":"spn-140022","text":" — queries routed to fast path"}]}],"id":"blk-77036","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77039","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140023","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.deliberate_count"},{"id":"spn-140024","text":" — queries routed to deliberation"}]}],"id":"blk-77038","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-77041","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140025","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.deliberate_ratio"},{"id":"spn-140026","text":" — deliberate / total (target: < 30% on typical workloads)"}]}],"id":"blk-77040","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-77042","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-140027","text":"7.3 BendScript Performance (JavaScript — "},{"id":"spn-140028","marks":["code"],"text":"performance.now()"},{"id":"spn-140029","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-77043","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"const t0 = performance.now();\nconst topo = analyzeTopology(plane);\nconst elapsed = performance.now() - t0;\nconsole.debug(`[κ] topology: ${elapsed.toFixed(1)}ms, maxκ=${topo.maxKappa}, sccs=${topo.sccCount}`);"},{"id":"blk-77044","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140030","text":"Target: < 50ms at 100 nodes."}]},{"id":"blk-77045","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-140031","marks":["italic"],"text":"Spec version: 0.2.0. Status: Draft (normalized). Depends on: kappa_reference.py (computation), kappa_theory_applied.md (theoretical foundations). Products affected: Graphonomous, Deliberatic, BendScript, [&] Protocol, TickTickClock, OpenSentience."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera7i5tknxbbx7opqp7gagy47pv6x4ffyy35wrstt4fcbmqoxececqa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}